course: dictionary
lesson: 10290
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings. Toss is one of them. The context, meaning the words around it, tells you which meaning the writer wants. «Cranes really dance, leaping, bowing, flapping and tossing sticks» shows that toss here means to throw something lightly, because birds throw sticks in the air, not because they are mixing or sleeping.
explain: Some meanings are fixed phrases. In «Think of a playground argument: you can toss a coin», the words coin and argument show that a coin toss is throwing a coin to settle a disagreement. The toss is a way to choose fairly, not a way to play catch.
explain: Test a meaning by putting it in the sentence. «Every bird there shows a different way to live: a toucan tosses a grape up and catches it.» Does «throws a grape up and catches it» still make sense? Yes, so that meaning is right. If your meaning does not fit, try another one from the list.
fact: To toss something means to throw it lightly, as in «toss the ball to me».
fact: A coin toss is throwing a coin to see whether heads or tails lands up.
fact: To toss a salad means to mix it gently, and to toss and turn means to move about in bed and not sleep.
fact: To toss something out means to throw it away.
fact: In maths, a coin has 2 sides, so heads and tails are equally likely. If you toss a coin 10 times and get 6 heads, then tails = 10 − 6 = 4.
exercise: «Every bird there shows a different way to live: a toucan tosses a grape up and catches it.» What does tosses mean here? | To sleep badly | To mix gently | *To throw lightly | To throw away
exercise: Sam says a coin toss decides who starts. What is a coin toss? | Counting the coins in a purse | Sorting coins by size | *Throwing a coin to see whether heads or tails lands up | Dropping a coin down a drain
exercise: «Saying something louder does not make it truer; if nobody saw clearly, agree a fair way to settle it, like a replay or a coin toss.» What is a coin toss used for in this sentence? | Hiding the truth | Choosing the best coin to keep | *To settle the argument fairly | Winning a prize for being loudest
test: At a fair in Texas, the hoop-toss hoops were just barely too small for the bottle necks. What is a hoop-toss? | A race to run around the fair | *A game of throwing hoops to land over bottles | Painting bottles in bright colours | Buying food from a stall
test: Ruby tosses a coin 10 times and it lands heads 6 times. How many times does it land tails? | 3 | 16 | *4 | 6
exam: Mum says, «Toss those old shoes out.» What does toss out mean? | To mix gently | *To throw away | To count carefully | To sleep badly
